-- Two exported decisions read an input called `rate` and give it different
-- TYPICALLY defaults. OpenFisca has one variable of that name and so one
-- default for it, and picking either would make the other decision wrong, so
-- the export refuses and names both.

@export Scaled amount
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled base rate MEANS base * rate

@export Capped amount
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
GIVETH A NUMBER
capped base rate MEANS (base * rate) - 1
